+### Turning Wiki Reads Off
+
+To stop agents from reading the wiki (to seed or inform their context), add this to `.ta/workflow.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[wiki]
+seed_context = false
+```
+
+The default is `true`, and a missing section or key means `true`. When it is `false`, the TA MCP gateway refuses `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` (including pages already in the local wiki cache), for goal agents and chat-mode sessions alike, and the daemon stops warming the wiki cache. The refusal names the setting and the file and tells you to set `seed_context = true` to turn reads back on.
+
+This is a read-side switch only. `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` keep working and still go through draft review. `ta doctor` prints a `Wiki reads` line while the switch is off. A value that is not `true` or `false` is an error that names `.ta/workflow.toml` and `seed_context`, and wiki reads are refused until you fix it.
+
 ### Wiki Writes Are Reviewed
 
 `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` do not write to the wiki when an agent calls them. They check the input and queue the change in the goal's draft. Nothing reaches Wayfinder until you approve and apply that draft. `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` are unchanged and read live.
